    rdf:value """charming and profound words ranted on the stage with conventional gestures, so we came away at the end of the first act. Philip and Lady Ottoline came in in [sic] the evening.
Saturday June 21. 1902.. London.
Bernhard went to the British Museum and I joined him there. We went on to the City and had a “Turtle lunch” with Burke. Bernhard went down to Dorking to the Trevelyans, and I went to bed with a raging headache.
Sunday June 22. 1902. .
Spent the day at Dorking with the Frys. Helen just recovering from her second baby - Pamela- but surprising and charming as ever. The Trevys came over too. Finished  Buckle , Bernhard finished  Bury’s History of Greece .  I have hardly ever enjoyed a book more than Buckle. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 55 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

